# Mac Studio API restart

Restarting the live Express API is **the agent’s job** when this Cursor instance is on **Yan’s Mac Studio** and the change set affects that process. Do not skip it or leave it for the user. Follow [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md).

Restarting the API is safe for running agents. Personal Agent turns live in a separate process, the agent worker (`com.personalagent.agent-worker`, `server/agent-worker.js`, 127.0.0.1:3005). The API proxies `/api/education/agent/*` and `/api/jype/agent/*` to it and re-attaches to the worker's status stream when it comes back, so loading dots and `/agent/running` pick up where they left off.

## Gate (must pass)

Confirm Mac Studio before any restart:

```bash
hostname | grep -qi 'Mac-Studio' || scutil --get ComputerName | grep -qi 'Mac Studio'
```

Skip restart on MacBook, Cursor Cloud, or any other host.

## Applicable changes

Restart the API when edits affect the running Node process, e.g. `server/**`, `server/package.json`, or `deploy/launchagents/com.personalagent.server.plist` / root `npm run server` plumbing. Do not wait for agents to go idle first.

Skip for static HTML/CSS/JS, iOS, Vercel-only, docs-only, or education/fitness data-folder sync.

## Restart command

```bash
launchctl kickstart -k "gui/$(id -u)/com.personalagent.server"
curl -sS -f http://127.0.0.1:3004/health
```

That LaunchAgent is the production equivalent of `npm run server`. If it is not loaded and a manual `npm run server` is running, stop it and start `npm run server` from the repo root instead, then verify `/health`.

## Agent worker restart (kills running turns)

Restart the worker only when the change touches code it runs: `server/personal-agent.js`, `server/agent-worker*.js`, `server/cursor-sdk-auth.js`, `server/future-agents.js`, the `*-agent-mentions.js` pollers, `*-mention.js`, `imessage-send.js` / `whatsapp-send.js` / `school-teams.js`, or another module `personal-agent.js` imports. Restarting it drops every in-flight Personal Agent turn and its queue, the same as an API restart did before.

Default to the idle restart. It waits until no chat is running or queued, then the worker exits and launchd starts the new code. Your own turn finishes first, so a Personal Agent turn can ask for it safely:

```bash
npm run agent-worker:restart-when-idle   # then: curl -sS http://127.0.0.1:3005/health
```

`launchctl kickstart -k "gui/$(id -u)/com.personalagent.agent-worker"` restarts at once and kills every running turn, yours included. Use it only from a plain terminal when `busySessions` is 0 or the fix is urgent.

If the worker LaunchAgent is not installed yet, run `deploy/launchagents/install-agent-worker.sh` once.
